    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\P(A_4|A_0) = \\frac{21}{81}"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ".",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "For ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "n = 5"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ", we'd again have to consider subgroups in our event space count: outcomes with ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "A_2"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ", ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "A_3"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ", or no intermediate As...  ",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": null,
    "level": "3",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Other Approaches: Code",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Brute-force enumeration via code is one hack to calculate these probabilities for higher ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "n"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ":",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "language": "python"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "def get_next_letter(letter, letters=[\"A\", \"C\", \"G\", \"T\"]):\n    # if \"A\", return \"C\"; if \"C\", return \"G\"; etc.\n    try:\n        return letters[letters.index(letter) + 1]\n    except:\n        # if here, we don't have a \"next letter\" (we're at T, the end)\n        return False\n\ndef get_next_outcome(outcome):\n    # recursive function for getting next possible mutation sequence\n    # ex: [\"A\", \"A\"] returns [\"A\", \"C\"]\n    #     [\"C\", \"T\"] returns [\"G\", \"A\"] (so the previous letter updates)\n    \n    next_letter = get_next_letter(outcome[-1])\n    if next_letter:\n        # if here, last letter was not T, so just increment last letter\n        return outcome[:-1] + [next_letter]\n    else:\n        # if here, the last letter was T, so we need to update multiple\n        # letters to make the next outcome (maybe do multiple recursions).\n        # like how in binary, 01011 + 1 -> 01100 (digits 1-3 updated)\n        next_outcome = get_next_outcome(outcome[:-1])\n        \n        # analogous to the new 0s in the binary example: when we update\n        # multiple letters, we put As where there were Ts at the end\n        return next_outcome + [\"A\"]\n\ndef any_consecutive_letters(outcome):\n    # check if an outcome follows the rule that no letters repeat consecutively\n    for i in range(len(outcome) - 1):\n        if outcome[i] == outcome[i+1]:\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef count_outcomes(n, start_letter=\"A\", end_event=\"A\"):\n    sample_space = 0  # |E|\n    event_space = 0   # |S|\n\n    # loop through all possible n-length sequences, starting with \"all As\"\n    outcome = [start_letter] + [\"A\"] * n\n    while True:\n        # end condition for get_next_outcome() iterating through all sequences\n        if outcome[0] != start_letter:\n            break\n\n        if not any_consecutive_letters(outcome): # is this outcome even valid?\n            sample_space += 1\n            if outcome[-1] == end_event: # if end letter is what we're looking for\n                event_space += 1\n\n        outcome = get_next_outcome(outcome)\n\n    return event_space / sample_space ",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "codeBlock"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": null,
    "level": "3",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Other Approaches: Recursion",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "If we really wanted to avoid counting event spaces, though, we could return to that aside from earlier. Recall the Law of Total Probability tells us (generalizing here):",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": ""
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\P(A_i|A_0) = \\P(C_{i-1}|A_0) = \\P(G_{i-1}|A_0) = \\P(T_{i-1}|A_0) \\\\\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "purpleBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "We can make this even more useful by observing that the probability of getting any of the four letters at a particular iteration must be 1, according to the second ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "class": null,
        "href": "https://{{pathToRoot}}/axioms",
        "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
        "target": "_blank"
       },
       "type": "link"
      }
     ],
     "text": "Axiom of Probability",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": ".",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n    \\P(A_{i-1} | A_0) + \\P(C_{i-1} | A_0) + \\P(G_{i-1} | A_0) + \\P(T_{i-1} | A_0) &= 1 \\\\\n    \\P(A_{i-1} | A_0) + \\P(C_{i-1} | A_0) + \\P(C_{i-1} | A_0) + \\P(C_{i-1} | A_0) &= 1 \\\\\n    \\P(A_{i-1} | A_0) + 3 \\P(C_{i-1} | A_0) &= 1 \\\\\n    \\P(C_{i-1} | A_0) &= \\frac{1}{3} (1 - \\P(A_{i-1} | A_0))\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "purpleBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Putting these together, we arrive at the following recursive relationship, which can be used to find ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\P(A_i|A_0)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " for any ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "i > 2"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ":",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n    \\P(A_i | A_0) = \\frac{1}{3} (1 - \\P(A_{i-1} | A_0))\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "purpleBox"
  },
